  "lineage": "Khmer sung theatre (lakhon yike) that enacts folk tales and legends through singing, dance and spoken passages, performed by village troupes and by the Royal University of Fine Arts. Its sound is led by the skor yike, a set of frame drums of graded sizes of which the largest is the skor mei, with traditional and modern melodic instruments completing the ensemble. The frame-drum card stands in for the skor yike and the tro sau card for the melodic instruments.",
